      "cwe_id": "CWE-89",
      "explanation": "The `status` parameter is taken directly from `request.args.get` and concatenated into a raw SQL string that is executed via `session.execute(text(query))`. This allows an attacker to inject arbitrary SQL commands (e.g., `status=' OR 1=1 --`).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "file": "app/routes/orders.py",
          "lines": [
            65,
            66
          ],
          "source": null,
          "content": "query = \"SELECT id, user_id, status, total FROM orders WHERE status = '\" + status + \"'\"\n    rows = session.execute(text(query))",
          "snapshot": null,
          "snapshot_conflict": false,
          "grounded_in_pr": true
        }
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Use parameterized queries. Replace the string concatenation with `text(\"SELECT id, user_id, status, total FROM orders WHERE status = :status\")` and pass `status` as a bound parameter: `session.execute(text(\"SELECT id, user_id, status, total FROM orders WHERE status = :status\"), {\"status\": status})`.",
